{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the covering of tachash that is upon it.</b> He did not also mention the covering of reddened ram skins, because they were joined one to the other, or the verse followed a shortened course." "<b>And the parashah.</b> This parashah explains the burden of the Levites and their service. For the burden of the sons of Gershon was light, for they carried the garments — and these are the curtains of the Tabernacle, the coverings, and the hangings. And this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory taught: the sons of Gershon were in charge of the implements of weaving. And behold, this is lighter service than that of Merari; but the sons of Merari — their service was heavy, for they were in charge of the bronze and the wood, which are the planks of the Tabernacle, its bars, its pillars, and its sockets. And it was stated: he was appointed over the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari, for when the Tabernacle was encamped they would return all the implements through him."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:21.421145686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}